# Ogera isolation (hard rule)

This repo is Ogera. It was forked from the Beyond Enterprise codebase, so it may still
contain names, docs, or history referring to **AlphaBridge** and **BeyondTechWorld**.
Those are separate live systems. Nothing done here may ever affect them.

## Never, under any circumstance

- Connect to, migrate, seed, dump-into, or drop the `beyondtech_laravel` or `alphabridge` databases
- Use the MySQL users `beyond` or `abt`
- Point `laravel-app/.env` or `apps/api/.env` at anything other than Ogera's own databases
- SSH to the VPS, or touch `/var/www/beyondtechworld`, `/var/www/alphabridge`, the
  `beyondtechworld-api` / `alphabridge-api` PM2 processes, or their nginx sites
- Push to `github.com/tefumbole/BeyondTechWorld` — `origin` here is `github.com/tefumbole/ogera`
- Re-add deploy tooling for those sites (it was deliberately deleted)

## Ogera's own resources

| Resource | Value |
|---|---|
| Laravel database | `ogera_laravel` |
| Node API database | `ogera` |
| MySQL user | `ogera` (privileges on those two databases only) |
| MySQL host | Homebrew MySQL, `127.0.0.1:3306` on the user's Mac |
| Git remote | `github.com/tefumbole/ogera` |

## Production

Ogera has no server yet, and the user has no VPS access at this time. Treat production as
off-limits by default: never deploy, rsync, scp, or run remote commands unless the user
explicitly asks. If a deploy is needed, give local-only steps or written instructions instead.

When Ogera does get a host, scope any new deploy script to that host alone and never
reuse the AlphaBridge or BeyondTechWorld paths, process names, or credentials.

## Local work that needs no permission

`npm run dev`, `npm run dev:api`, `npm run dev:local`, `npm run db:migrate`,
`npm run local:backup`, `bash tools/setup-ogera-db.sh`, local Docker MySQL on port 3307.
